the path to the chernobyl power plant is  barren overgrown and lonesome this  amusement park nearby was due to open  five days after the 1986 nuclear  meltdown whose name is now synonymous  with disaster  it never did  36 years later radiation levels are  still well above normal in some places  that's high  visoka  the reading is about 16 times normal  inside explosion ravaged reactor number  four now shrouded by a large container  radiation levels remain high  vladimir vurbitsky still a chernobyl  engineer rushed to the plant the day of  the meltdown  when i got there i was expecting to see  the reactor  what i saw was the crater left by the  explosion  with the zapariza nuclear plant taking  fire repeatedly in front line fighting  in southern ukraine locals say it could  pose an even greater danger  i worked at chernobyl and i witnessed  the tragic consequences of the explosion  zapariza could be two three four times  bigger than chernobyl and i'm very  worried about that  believe it or not this is the center of  the town of prippet that's the cultural  building behind me on the day after the  meltdown at chernobyl all 50 000  residents were evacuated and not a soul  has lived here since  now nature has reclaimed the landscape  on which prepit was built  the president of the company that owns  the zaparisia plant says russian forces  have placed trucks and explosives inside  turbine holds near the reactor and are  firing from the plant's grounds russia  blames ukraine for the strikes on the  plant it is an act of nuclear terrorism  and they continue in this way  unlike chernobyl vladimir furbitsky says  zaparisia is europe's biggest nuclear  plant and it lies in a heavily populated  region  this won't happen in russia the west  will feel the consequences bulgaria  romania moldova and poland  he hopes both russia and ukraine have  learned the lessons of chernobyl so the  land that surrounds zapposia doesn't  also become a nuclear wasteland for  decades to come john hendren al jazeera  the chernobyl exclusion zone ukraine
 

